Li$_{3}$PS$_{4}$ is known to exist in four forms (Homma, 2011): \begin{itemize} \item $\gamma$-Li$_{3}$PS$_{4}$, the ground state, is stable below 573K in the \href{current_web_home_dir/AB3C4_oP16_31_a_ab_2ab-001}{enargite ($H2_{5}$) structure}. \item \href{current_web_home_dir/A4BC4_oP36_62_acd_c_2cd-001}{$\beta$-Li$_{3}$PS$_{4}$} (this structure) is stable between 573 and 746K. \item \href{current_web_home_dir/A2BC4_oP28_60_d_c_2d-002}{$\alpha$-Li$_{3}$PS$_{4}$} is stable above 746K. \item \href{current_web_home_dir/A3BC4_tP16_114_ad_b_e-001}{$\delta$-Li$_{3}$PS$_{4}$} is a predicted high-pressure phase. \end{itemize} ~ \vspace{-.25in} 
 Data for $\beta$-Li$_{3}$PS$_{4}$ was taken at 637K. The Li I (4a) site is 70\% occupied, while the Li II (4c) site is 30\% occupied. 
 AFLOW shifts the origin by c/2 along the $\hat{z}$-axis, moving the Li I atoms from the (4b) to the (4a) Wyckoff positions.
